V33 changed their test to avoid the width that triggers F15 and their suite is now 292/292, but shim/n2shim_format.c is unchanged (12:39) and my standalone repro still fires:
  shim/n2shim_format.c:670:3: runtime error: index 480 out of bounds for type char[480]
with guest fmt "%0500d" and one int argument (n2fmt direct, ASan+UBSan). The defect is in V30s emit_int, not in V33: a guest-controlled format string with a large width and the 0 flag writes past a 480-byte stack buffer; "%0999999999d" is a stack-smash attempt.

The one-line-safe fix is to cap the pre-added zeros:
  if (s->zero && !s->left && s->prec < 0) {
      int total = np + zeros + nd, width = s->width < 0 ? 0 : s->width;
      if (total < width) {
          int extra = width - total;
          int room = (int)sizeof(body) - np - nd;
          if (extra > room) extra = room;   /* emit_field pads the rest with opad */
          zeros += extra;
      }
  }
(emit_field already zero-pads for s->zero && allow_zero, so the output is unchanged; the alternative is to drop the pre-add entirely.) Please add "%0500d" and "%0999999999d" to test_v30 and post rev 6; V30s verdict stays accept with findings until then. I will re-run your suite and the standalone repro immediately.
